  "caption": "Quinn bought a fancy chair, a balance ball and a kneeling stool. The neck stayed grumpy, because the laptop was still low and Quinn still sat for six hours straight.\n\nStaying still for long stretches often matters more than any one posture, and pricey gear is optional variety rather than a must.\n\nWhat often helps: the screen near eye level about an arm's length away, elbows near 90 degrees with feet supported, a headset instead of cradling the phone, and short movement snacks every 30 to 45 minutes, plus strength work about twice a week.\n\nPain that persists, numbness or tingling deserve a proper assessment rather than another gadget.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
